@startuml

title Auto-approval: the rule a raise is closed under

start
:A request is raised;
if (The request names parts?) then (yes)
  :Wait for the people\nwho answer the parts;
  stop
endif
:Read the provisioning grants and the\napprovals mode, before the raise's\ntransaction, for the whole tenant;
if (A provisioning run holds an unexpired\ngrant for the request's kind?) then (yes)
  :Approve under the rule **provisioning**;
  stop
endif
if (The tenant states a mode?) then (yes)
  if (Tenant mode is auto_approved?) then (yes)
    :Approve under the rule **tenant**;
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  if (Installation mode is auto_approved?) then (yes)
    :Approve under the rule **deployment**;
    stop
  endif
endif
if (The kind's code is every_request?) then (yes)
  :Approve under the rule **every_request**;
  stop
endif
if (The kind's code is system_tenant\nand the request is the system tenant's?) then (yes)
  :Approve under the rule **system_tenant**;
  stop
endif
:Wait for a person;
note right
  A mode that cannot be read
  is read as enforced.
  A rule never passes a candidate
  that failed a blocking check:
  the raise refuses it first.
end note
stop

@enduml
